Q.Difference between queue and topic
Queues are primarily used for point-to-point communication, where a single consumer processes messages from a queue.
Topics are used for publish-subscribe scenarios, where messages are broadcast to multiple subscribers interested in the topic.

Difference between Exclusive and non Exclusive?
Exclusive:
Single consumer, order preservation, suitable for transactional applications.
Non-Exclusive:
Multiple consumers, load balancing, suitable for applications that can handle multiple parallel processing instances.

how to see payloads in solace?
To see message payloads in Solace, you can use the Solace Brocker Manager or a Solace queue browser. These tools allow you to view messages, including their payloads, without consuming them.
Using the Broker Manager:
Navigate to Queues: In the Broker Manager, go to "Queues" in the left navigation bar.
Select a Queue: Choose the specific queue you want to inspect.
Browse Messages: The Broker Manager will display messages in the queue, and you can view their payloads






